    "summary": "Jerry's 40th birthday at the Zoo delivers a scorching Playin > Iko jam and high‑energy second set.",
    "review": "On August 1, 1982 the Dead turned the Oklahoma City Zoo Amphitheater into a birthday party for Jerry.  The heat was brutal in the first set – you can hear the band fighting through it on tracks like “China Cat Sunflower” and “C.C. Rider” – but by the second set they were totally locked in, rolling straight from an inspired “Playing In The Band” into a searing “Iko Iko” jam that has become the highlight of this night.  From there the energy never let up: “Space > The Wheel”, a soulful “Black Peter”, and a rollicking “Around & Around” keep the crowd dancing, while Jerry’s lead on “Tennessee Jed” and his sweet phrasing on “They Love Each Other” remind everyone why it was his 40th birthday.  The show is high‑energy throughout, with Phil’s bass turned up in places, Bill and Mickey laying down a solid groove, and Brent adding the usual tasteful keys texture.\n\nIf you want to hear this night at its best, the Willy soundboard (gd82-08-01.sbd.willy.10226.sbeok.shnf) captures the band’s chemistry with clear mids, audible bass and just enough of the summer heat in the background to give it that authentic Zoo feel without drowning out any instrument.  It’s a solid, well‑balanced tape that lets you ride every transition – especially that monster “Playin > Iko” sequence.",
